[38;5;16m[48;5;153m ☐ Approach [39m[49m

[1m[38;5;231mWhich approach should the design use?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mA: schema registry (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mDeclared prefs with centralized defaults + validation, one namespaced localStorage key per preference, per-value [39m
     [38;5;246mversion marker.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m B: single JSON document
     [38;5;246mAll prefs in one versioned key. Cleanest migrations and export/import, but whole-document writes and cross-tab [39m
     [38;5;246mclobber risk.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m C: thin key/value wrapper
     [38;5;246mSmallest possible module, defaults at call sites, no validation or versioning. Cheapest now, drifts as settings [39m
     [38;5;246mmultiply.[39m
  [38;5;246m4. Type something.[39m
